VERDICT: needs-changes
{"verdict":"needs-changes","summary":"The change avoids clearing the top gap but still redraws the same visible history tail lower in the terminal after a shrink, leaving stale duplicate copies above the redraw span. This is a correctness regression in the repaint lifecycle for moved-down viewports.","findings":[{"file":"crates/mu-solo/src/viewport.rs","line":648,"severity":"medium","issue":"When the viewport shrinks and moves down, the existing screen rows above the old viewport still contain the same screen-resident history tail at their old coordinates. This change stops clearing rows `0..top`, but the subsequent draw loop still repaints `self.history[start..]` beginning at `top`, so rows `0..top` retain stale copies of the first redrawn history lines while the same lines are drawn again lower down. For example, with `history_len=100`, old `viewport.y=30`, new `visible_rows=40`, and `scrollback_committed=70`, rows 0..30 already contain history 70..100; repaint draws history 70..100 into rows 10..40, leaving rows 0..10 as duplicate stale history rather than a valid non-redrawn region."}]}
